#: ../../../global_options.rst:2
msgid "Global options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:4
msgid ""
"The following options can be set for all tasks in a project directly under "
"``[tool.poe]``. These are called global options, in contrast with :doc:`task "
"options<tasks/options>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:6
msgid "**env** : ``dict[str, str]`` :ref:`📖<Global environment variables>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:5 ../../../global_options.rst:26
msgid "dict[str, str] 📖"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:7
msgid ""
"Define environment variables to be exposed to all tasks. These can be :ref:"
"`extended on the task level<Setting task specific environment variables>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:9
msgid ""
"**envfile** : ``str`` | ``list[str]`` :ref:`📖<Global environment variables>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:8 ../../../global_options.rst:20
#: ../../../global_options.rst:190 ../../../global_options.rst:193
#: ../../../global_options.rst:196 ../../../global_options.rst:199
msgid "str | list[str] 📖"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:10
msgid ""
"Link to one or more files defining environment variables to be exposed to "
"all tasks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:12
msgid ""
"**executor** : ``str`` | ``dict[str, str]`` :ref:`📖<Configure the executor>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:11
msgid "str | dict[str, str] 📖"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:13
msgid ""
"Specify the default executor type and/or configuration for all tasks in this "
"project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:15
msgid ""
"**include** : ``str`` | ``dict[str, str]`` | ``list[str | dict[str, str]]`` "
"| :doc:`📖<../guides/include_guide>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:14
msgid "str | dict[str, str] | list[str | dict[str, str]] | 📖"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:16
msgid ""
"Specify one or more other toml or json files to load tasks from. By default "
"includes are followed recursively, unless the ``recursive`` option is set to "
"``false`` for a specific include."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:18
msgid ""
"**include_script** : ``str`` | ``dict[str, str]`` | ``list[str | dict[str, "
"str]]`` :doc:`📖<../guides/packaged_tasks>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:17
msgid "str | dict[str, str] | list[str | dict[str, str]] 📖"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:19
msgid ""
"Load dynamically generated tasks from one or more python functions. This is "
"similar to the :doc:`include global option<../guides/include_guide>`, except "
"instead of providing paths to config files, one can reference python "
"functions that generate task config, using the same syntax as for :doc:"
"`script tasks<../tasks/task_types/script>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:21
msgid ""
"**shell_interpreter** : ``str`` | ``list[str]`` :ref:`📖<Change the default "
"shell interpreter>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:22
msgid ""
"Change the default interpreter to use for executing :doc:`shell tasks<../"
"tasks/task_types/shell>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:24
msgid "**poetry_command** : ``str`` :ref:`📖<Configuring the plugin>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:23 ../../../global_options.rst:220
msgid "str 📖"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:25
msgid ""
"Change the name of the task poe registers with poetry when used as a plugin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:27
msgid ""
"**poetry_hooks** : ``dict[str, str]`` :ref:`📖<Hooking into poetry commands>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:28
msgid ""
"Register tasks to run automatically before or after other poetry CLI "
"commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:30
msgid "**verbosity** : ``int``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:29
msgid "int"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:31
msgid ""
"Set the default verbosity level for tasks in this project. The default value "
"is ``0``, providing the ``-v`` global CLI option increases it by ``1``, "
"whereas the ``-q`` global CLI option decreases it by ``1``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:33
msgid ""
"**default_task_type** : ``\"cmd\" | \"expr\" | \"ref\" | \"script\" | "
"\"shell\"``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:32 ../../../global_options.rst:38
msgid "\"cmd\" | \"expr\" | \"ref\" | \"script\" | \"shell\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:34
msgid ""
"When a task is declared as a string (instead of a table), then it is "
"interpreted as the default task type, which will be ``\"cmd\"`` unless "
"otherwise specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:36
msgid "**default_array_task_type** : ``str``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:35
msgid "str"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:37
msgid ""
"When a task is declared as an array (instead of a table), then it is "
"interpreted as the default array task type, which will be ``\"sequence\"`` "
"unless otherwise specified. Valid options are ``\"sequence\"`` or "
"``\"parallel\"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:39
msgid ""
"**default_array_item_task_type** : ``\"cmd\" | \"expr\" | \"ref\" | "
"\"script\" | \"shell\"``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:40
msgid ""
"When a task is declared as a string inside an array (e.g. inline in a "
"sequence task), then it is interpreted as the default array item task type, "
"which will be ``\"ref\"`` unless otherwise specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:43
msgid "Global environment variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:45
msgid ""
"You can configure environment variables to be set for all poe tasks in the "
"pyproject.toml file by specifying :toml:`tool.poe.env` like so"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:47
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.env]\n"
"VAR1 = \"FOO\"\n"
"VAR2 = \"BAR BAR BLACK ${FARM_ANIMAL}\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:53
msgid ""
"The example above also demonstrates how – as with env vars defined at the "
"task level – posix variable interpolation syntax may be used to define "
"global env vars with reference to variables already defined in the host "
"environment or in a referenced env file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:55
msgid ""
"As with the task level option, you can indicated that a variable should only "
"be set if not already set like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:57
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.env]\n"
"VAR1.default = \"FOO\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:63
msgid "Loading external environment variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:65
msgid ""
"You can also specify an env file (with bash-like syntax) to load for all "
"tasks like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:67
msgid ".env"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:67
msgid ""
" STAGE=dev\n"
" PASSWORD='!@#$%^&*('"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:73
msgid "pyproject.toml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:73
msgid ""
" [tool.poe]\n"
" envfile = \".env\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:79
msgid "The envfile global option also accepts a list of env files like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:81
msgid ""
"[tool.poe]\n"
"envfile = [\"standard.env\", \"local.env\"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:86
msgid "In this case the referenced files will be loaded in the given order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:90
msgid ""
"The envfile option is also available with the same capabilities at :ref:`the "
"task level<Loading environment variables from an env file>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:93
msgid "Parameter expansion in env files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:95
msgid ""
"Env file values support bash-style parameter expansion. Each variable can "
"reference variables defined earlier in the same file using ``$VAR`` or "
"``${VAR}``, as well as variables already set in the environment (host env "
"vars, global env, or parent task env vars). The standard default/alternate "
"operators are supported:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:97
msgid ""
"BASE=/opt/myapp\n"
"DATA_DIR=${BASE}/data         # expands to /opt/myapp/data\n"
"LOG_DIR=${BASE}/logs          # expands to /opt/myapp/logs\n"
"\n"
"# Use a default when a variable is unset\n"
"HOST=${APP_HOST:-localhost}\n"
"\n"
"# Use an alternate value when a variable is set\n"
"DEBUG_FLAG=${DEBUG:+--debug}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:109
msgid ""
"Expansion is applied in unquoted values and inside double-quoted values. "
"Single-quoted values are never expanded — ``'${VAR}'`` is always the literal "
"string ``${VAR}``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:112
msgid "Optional env files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:114
msgid ""
"Normally poe will emit a warning if a specified envfile is not found. If you "
"consider an envfile to be optional, you can suppress these warnings by "
"configuring the file path (or paths) under the ``optional`` prefix like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:116
msgid ""
"[tool.poe]\n"
"envfile.optional = \".env\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:121
msgid "You can combine optional and expected envfiles like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:123
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.envfile]\n"
"expected = [\"shared.env\"]\n"
"optional = [\"local.env\"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:129
msgid ""
"In this example ``shared.env`` is considered mandatory, whereas ``local."
"env`` may be absent without generating noise. Using :toml:`envfile = \"."
"env\"` remains equivalent to setting :toml:`envfile.expected = \".env\"` "
"explicitly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:132
msgid "Resolving env file paths"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:134
msgid ""
"Normally envfile paths are resolved relative to the project root (that is "
"the parent directory of the pyproject.toml). However when working with a "
"monorepo it can also be useful to specify the path relative to the root of "
"the git repository, which can be done by referencing the ``POE_GIT_DIR`` or "
"``POE_GIT_ROOT`` variables like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:136
msgid ""
"[tool.poe]\n"
"envfile = \"${POE_GIT_DIR}/.env\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:141
msgid ""
"See the documentation on :ref:`Special variables<Special variables>` for a "
"full explanation of how these variables work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:145
msgid ""
"Environment variables loaded from env files have higher precedence than any "
"inherited from the host environment, but lower precedence than env defined "
"directly in the pyproject.toml file. Similarly ``optional`` env files are "
"loaded after ``expected`` ones, so variables defined in ``optional`` files "
"can override those defined in ``expected`` files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:147
msgid ""
"During parameter expansion within an env file, variables from lower-"
"precedence sources (host env, previously loaded env files, and task-level "
"env vars set before this file is loaded) are visible and can be referenced. "
"In-file definitions always take precedence over these during expansion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:151
msgid "Configure the executor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:153
msgid ""
"You can configure poe to use a specific executor by setting :toml:`tool.poe."
"executor`. Valid values include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:156
msgid ""
"**auto**: to automatically use the most appropriate of the following "
"executors in order"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:157
msgid "**poetry**: to run tasks in the poetry managed environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:158
msgid "**uv**: to run tasks in an uv environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:159
msgid ""
"**virtualenv**: to run tasks in the indicated virtualenv (or else \"./."
"venv\" or \"./venv\" if present)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:160
msgid "**simple**: to run tasks without doing any specific environment setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:162
msgid "The default behavior is **auto**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:164
msgid ""
"You specify a different executor to use as a global option, task level "
"option, or at runtime with the ``--executor`` cli option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:166
msgid ""
"For example you can make your whole project use the simple executor (no "
"environment integration) by default like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:168
msgid ""
"[tool.poe]\n"
"executor = \"simple\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:173
msgid ""
"Which is a short hand for the following table form which is required in "
"order to pass options to the executor:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:175
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.executor]\n"
"type = \"simple\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:182
msgid ""
"You can also configure the executor at the :ref:`task group level<Grouping "
"tasks>`, or at the :ref:`task level<Configure the executor for a task>`, "
"which will have higher precedence. Alternatively you can override the "
"executor type at runtime by passing the ``--executor`` CLI option (before "
"the task name) with the name of the executor to use, and pass executor "
"options via the ``--executor-opt`` global CLI option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:187
msgid "Uv Executor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:189
msgid ""
"The uv executor can be configured with the following options, which "
"translate into passing the corresponding CLI option to the `uv run command "
"<https://docs.astral.sh/uv/reference/cli/#uv-run>`_:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:191
msgid ""
"**extra** : ``str`` | ``list[str]`` `📖 <https://docs.astral.sh/uv/reference/"
"cli/#uv-run--extra>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:192
msgid "Include optional dependencies from the specified extra name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:194
msgid ""
"**group** : ``str`` | ``list[str]`` `📖 <https://docs.astral.sh/uv/reference/"
"cli/#uv-run--group>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:195
msgid "Include dependencies from the specified dependency group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:197
msgid ""
"**no-group** : ``str`` | ``list[str]`` `📖 <https://docs.astral.sh/uv/"
"reference/cli/#uv-run--no-group>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:198
msgid "Disable the specified dependency group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:200
msgid ""
"**with** : ``str`` | ``list[str]`` `📖 <https://docs.astral.sh/uv/reference/"
"cli/#uv-run--with>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:201
msgid "Run with the given packages installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:203
msgid ""
"**isolated** : ``bool`` `📖 <https://docs.astral.sh/uv/reference/cli/#uv-"
"run--isolated>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:202 ../../../global_options.rst:205
#: ../../../global_options.rst:208 ../../../global_options.rst:211
#: ../../../global_options.rst:214 ../../../global_options.rst:217
msgid "bool 📖"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:204
msgid ""
"Run the command in a fresh emphemeral virtual environment, instead of the "
"usual in-project .venv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:206
msgid ""
"**exact** : ``bool`` `📖 <https://docs.astral.sh/uv/reference/cli/#uv-run--"
"exact>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:207
msgid ""
"Sync the environment exactly, removing extraneous packages not in the "
"requested groups (unlike the default inexact sync which only adds missing "
"packages)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:209
msgid ""
"**no-sync** : ``bool`` `📖 <https://docs.astral.sh/uv/reference/cli/#uv-run--"
"no-sync>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:210
msgid "Avoid syncing the virtual environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:212
msgid ""
"**locked** : ``bool`` `📖 <https://docs.astral.sh/uv/reference/cli/#uv-run--"
"locked>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:213 ../../../global_options.rst:216
msgid "Run without updating the uv.lock file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:215
msgid ""
"**frozen** : ``bool`` `📖 <https://docs.astral.sh/uv/reference/cli/#uv-run--"
"frozen>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:218
msgid ""
"**no-project** : ``bool`` `📖 <https://docs.astral.sh/uv/reference/cli/#uv-"
"run--no-project>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:219
msgid "Avoid discovering the project or workspace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:221
msgid ""
"**python** : ``str`` `📖 <https://docs.astral.sh/uv/reference/cli/#uv-run--"
"python>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:222
msgid "The Python interpreter to use for the run environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:224
msgid ""
"You can combine project and task level executor options and inheritance will "
"work as you would expect:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:226
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.executor]\n"
"type = \"uv\"\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.tasks.test-py311]\n"
"cmd = \"pytest tests\"\n"
"executor = {isolated = true, python = \"3.11\", with = [\"pytest\"]}\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.tasks.test-py312]\n"
"cmd = \"pytest tests\"\n"
"executor = {isolated = true, python = \"3.12\", with = [\"pytest\"]}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:239
msgid ""
"This feature enables you to replace tools like tox by creating task variants "
"for different Python versions or environments. See the :doc:`../guides/"
"tox_replacement_guide` for a detailed guide on using poethepoet in this way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:241
msgid ""
"This kind of task level executor config will even work seamlessly in "
"projects that don't otherwise use `uv` if the executor type is specified at "
"the task level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:244
msgid "Virtualenv Executor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:246
msgid "The virtualenv executor can be configured with the following options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:248
msgid "**location** : ``bool``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:247
msgid "bool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:249
msgid ""
"The path of the virtual environment to use. Defaults to ``./venv`` or ``./."
"venv``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:251
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.executor]\n"
"type = \"virtualenv\"\n"
"location = \"myvenv\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:257
msgid ""
"If the virtualenv location is a relative path then it is resolved relative "
"to the project root (the parent directory of the pyproject.toml file. "
"However in a monorepo project it may also be defined relative to the git "
"repo root by templating :ref:`these  special environment variables<Special "
"variables>` like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:259
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.executor]\n"
"type = \"virtualenv\"\n"
"location = \"${POE_GIT_DIR}/myvenv\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:267
msgid "Change the default shell interpreter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:269
msgid ""
"Normally shell tasks are executed using a posix shell by default (see "
"section for shell tasks above). This default can be overridden to something "
"else by setting the *shell_interpreter* global option. In the following "
"example we configure all shell tasks to use *fish* by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:274
msgid ""
"tool.poe.shell_interpreter = \"fish\"\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.tasks.fibonacci]\n"
"help = \"Output the fibonacci sequence up to 89\"\n"
"shell = \"\"\"\n"
"  function fib --argument-names max n0 n1\n"
"    if test $max -ge $n0\n"
"      echo $n0\n"
"      fib $max $n1 (math $n0 + $n1)\n"
"    end\n"
"  end\n"
"\n"
"  fib 89 1 1\n"
"\"\"\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:292
msgid "Default command verbosity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:294
msgid ""
"You can alter the verbosity level for poe commands by passing :bash:`--"
"quiet` / :bash:`-q` (which decreases verbosity) or :bash:`--verbose` / :bash:"
"`-v` (which increases verbosity) on the CLI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:298
msgid ""
"If you want to change the default verbosity level for all commands, you can "
"use the :toml:`tool.poe.verbose` option in pyproject.toml like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:301
msgid ""
"[tool.poe]\n"
"verbosity = -1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:306
msgid ""
":toml:`-1` is the quietest and :toml:`1` is the most verbose. :toml:`0` is "
"the default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:309
msgid ""
"Note that the command line arguments are incremental: :bash:`-q` subtracts "
"one from the default verbosity, and :bash:`-v` adds one. So setting the "
"default verbosity to :toml:`-1` and passing :bash:`-v -v` on the command "
"line is equivalent to setting the verbosity to :toml:`0` and just passing :"
"bash:`-v`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:315
msgid "Change the default task type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:317
msgid ""
"By default tasks defined as strings are interpreted as shell commands, and "
"script tasks require the more verbose table syntax to specify. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:320
msgid ""
"my_cmd_task = \"cmd args\"\n"
"my_script_task = { \"script\" = \"my_package.my_module:run\" }"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:325
msgid ""
"This behaviour can be reversed by setting the :toml:`default_task_type` "
"option in your pyproject.toml like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:328
msgid ""
"[tool.poe]\n"
"default_task_type = \"script\"\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.tasks]\n"
"my_cmd_task = { \"cmd\" = \"cmd args\" }\n"
"my_script_task = \"my_package.my_module:run\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:338
msgid "Run poe from anywhere"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:340
msgid ""
"By default poe will detect when you're inside a project with a pyproject."
"toml in the root. However if you want to run it from elsewhere then that is "
"supported by using the :bash:`-C` option to specify an alternate location "
"for the toml file. The task will run with the given location as the current "
"working directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../global_options.rst:345
msgid ""
"In all cases the path to project root (where the pyproject.toml resides) "
"will be available as :bash:`$POE_ROOT` within the command line and process."
msgstr ""
